mespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":35171,"output_tokens":1090,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"89c58a78c8e69fa578df91b72df6d009bc2ab592d8ad3ae43a17b2cae845ae30"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":85438,"output_tokens":4749,"requests":6}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"9cdbfd2689f3889c2783af1a556afa9ab3496cc0054151f6e6dfddd7a352490c"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":72497,"output_tokens":3998,"requests":6}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In AC5, state how assert_volumes_in_service.py obtains the LIVE host mount table at runtime (e.g. SSM SendCommand run under the operator's credentials from runbook §10, or an explicit mount-table input file), and specify that a failed/denied host probe is a distinct outcome from UNKNOWN rather than collapsing into it.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.264,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC5: 'It joins the two halves nobody had joined -- terraform's aws_volume_attachment set against the host's mount table'","AC7 establishes the host probe requires ssm:SendCommand which the plan role lacks (iam.tf ReadOnlyAccess + kms:Decrypt confirmed at iam.tf:176-193)","AC5 names only an OFFLINE oracle test (test_assert_volumes_in_service_dcc3.py); the runtime source of the live mount table is not stated","ABSENCE: the three-valued UNKNOWN outcome is defined as 'the host did not report the device' but the plan does not say how the script queries the host, so it is unclear whether a failed/denied SSM call also collapses into UNKNOWN vs a distinct error"],"finding":"AC5's runtime data-flow is under-specified: the script must join terraform's attachment set against the LIVE host mount table, but the plan never states how the real (non-test) invocation acquires that mount table, given the plan itself establishes that reading it requires ssm:SendCommand (a write action). AC7 implies operator-run invocation supplies the SSM credential path, but AC5 does not name the mechanism (SSM SendCommand? a snapshotted lsblk/mount input file?) nor how UNKNOWN is distinguished from a failed SSM call.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9d314107df00887a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, AC5 (scripts/assert_volumes_in_service.py)","norm_id":"ne90aa5f4dfe4f49b","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer builds the join against terraform state but hard-codes or omits the live-host input, producing a script that cannot actually detect the attached-but-unmounted condition on the running box","SSM SendCommand is denied at runtime and the script silently reports UNKNOWN (looks benign) rather than a distinct probe-failure, re-introducing the same silent-fallback class the ticket exists to close"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC5 that the real invocation reads the host mount table via `ssm send-command` executed by the operator (the same credentials that ran the runbook), passing device/mount output to the script; keep the offline oracle test feeding a captured mount table. Define four dispositions explicitly: IN-SERVICE (pass), NOT-IN-SERVICE (fail, name volume), UNKNOWN=host did not report the device (fail), and PROBE-ERROR=host query failed/denied (fail, distinct message) so a denied SSM call cannot read as benign.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In AC5/AC7, state the concrete runtime mechanism by which assert_volumes_in_service.py obtains the LIVE host mount table (e.g. operator-credentialed `ssm:SendCommand`, or reading a host-published probe artifact, or executing on-host), including which identity/credentials it runs under, so the host-side half of the join is feasibility-verified and not just the terraform-parse half.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.364,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC5: 'It joins the two halves nobody had joined -- terraform's aws_volume_attachment set against the host's mount table'","AC5 defines three outcomes including 'UNKNOWN (the host did not report the device)' — which presupposes a live host read but names no transport","AC7 specifies only WHEN it runs ('MANDATORY post-apply step, invoked from infra/runbooks/gate-scratch-mount.md §10') and why it is not in terraform-drift.yml (the plan OIDC role lacks ssm:SendCommand — confirmed at iam.tf:176-193 and terraform-drift.yml:7-9), but not HOW the script reaches the host","The offline oracle test tests/unit/test_assert_volumes_in_service_dcc3.py covers the terraform-parse half; the live host-table acquisition is exactly the surface an offline test cannot exercise","Evidence class: Partially-verified — terraform-attachment side is feasible/offline-testable; live host-mount-table acquisition is Unverified for lack of a stated mechanism"],"finding":"AC5's assert_volumes_in_service.py asserts it joins terraform's aws_volume_attachment set against the LIVE host mount table (and distinguishes UNKNOWN = 'the host did not report the device'), but the plan never states the runtime mechanism by which the script obtains that live host-side mount data.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffb27daf487b210c9","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — AC5 and AC7 ('Invocation point, stated')","norm_id":"n7b7eea4e32663f55","priority":0.536,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author implements the terraform-parse half against the offline oracle, ships, and the host-side read has no defined transport — the script either can't run against the live host or silently reports UNKNOWN for every volume","Operator runs the §10 step post-apply and the script has no credentials/path to reach the host, so the delivery-gap check it was written to be does not actually check delivery"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to AC5 (or AC7's 'Invocation point') naming the transport — most naturally 'run under the operator's own credentials via `aws ssm send-command` (which ReadOnlyAccess-limited CI cannot do, per the terraform-drift rationale), capturing the host's mount table into the script's input' — and cover that the transport can distinguish a genuine 'device not reported' (UNKNOWN) from an SSM/probe failure.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reach